Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/coffgen.c
Line: 2241
Function: coff_print_symbol
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: The loop over auxiliary entries uses combined->u.syment.n_numaux to index into the raw symbol array without verifying bounds. It computes auxp = combined + aux + 1 and then dereferences auxp (e.g., auxp->is_sym) without checking that auxp < obj_raw_syments(abfd) + obj_raw_syment_count. A crafted COFF file with an oversized n_numaux can cause auxp to point past the end of the array, leading to an out-of-bounds read when printing symbols (bfd_print_symbol_all).

